    "basis": "Retained Protomaps 20261020 footprints and 201 × 201 Mapzen Terrarium samples at 6 m spacing establish the signed pose and the uncovered 36.63 m courtyard datum. The bounded museum grade corrects elevation bleed from the Kupfergraben across the two wing ends. The entrance floor stands 0.90 m above the court; a gently sloped apron meets the forecourt. A masonry quay closes the bank between and below the wing ends at the mapped canal edge. Water polygons, roads, and neighboring buildings remain native. The grade, apron dimensions and quay profile are visualization approximations."
