  "note": "Q157298 and named PMTiles way313659704/native35184685748536 establish the museum. Integral ways231549083/084/085/086/087 identify main hall, south wing, east service alcove, vestibule and north wing. Internal+X follows the mapped south-southeast front edge between wing ends; +Z points west-southwest through the open courtyard toward Kupfergraben. Heading0 with orientation baked into east/south geometry. Do not remove independent James-Simon-Galerie way194422265, Neues Museum way18578139, Bode Museum relation4211594 or neighboring colonnades. Retained Protomaps 20261020 footprints and 201 × 201 Mapzen Terrarium samples at 6 m spacing establish the signed pose and the uncovered 36.63 m courtyard datum. The bounded museum grade corrects elevation bleed from the Kupfergraben across the two wing ends. The entrance floor stands 0.90 m above the court; a gently sloped apron meets the forecourt. A masonry quay closes the bank between and below the wing ends at the mapped canal edge. Water polygons, roads, and neighboring buildings remain native. The grade, apron dimensions and quay profile are visualization approximations. The entrance appearance is registered for the date of the reference photograph. Native surroundings are current map data. Historical placement requires an explicit viewingDate within the recorded appearance interval; excluded from the default current world."
